# openOODA — governance
File: website/pulled/openOODA.oot

Source: openOODA/openOODA/

## What it is

The governance repo. Process boards, RFCs, and the 23 laws.
No compiler code lives here. Agent front door is `ANCHOR.oo`.

Read order: RULES.oot, NORTHSTAR.oot, rfcs/ANCHOR.oo,
practices/ANCHOR.oo.

## Install

```
curl -fsSL https://openooda.org/install.sh | bash
```

## Surface

Twelve repos. Git tags as of 2026-09-04.

| Repo | Role | Tag |
|------|------|-----|
| openOODA | Laws, RFCs, practices | v1.0.20 |
| oodac | Compiler | v0.2.2 |
| oodar | Gen 1 C host | v4.0.0 |
| std | Standard library | v1.0.8 |
| ooda | `ooda` driver | v0.2.7 |
| opm | Package manager | v0.8.8 |
| catalog | Public package list | — |
| lsp | Language server | v0.6.12 |
| mcp | MCP server | v0.6.10 |
| website | openooda.org | v1.2.10 |
| packaging | apt, dnf, pacman | v0.1.6 |
| .github | Org profile | — |

The compiler is the substrate. The other repos are siblings.
Governance edits must not trigger compiler rebuilds.
Directory topology stays still: Delta_path = 0.
